## 15. Required Testing and Completion Criteria

Before declaring the application complete, run and fix the available build checks and tests.

Verify the following end-to-end workflows:

1. Create or sign in to an account using the configured authentication method.
2. Send a message and receive a real Gemini-generated response.
3. Refresh the page and verify that chat history is retained.
4. Rename, search, and delete a conversation.
5. Create a project and save conversations to it.
6. Upload a supported document and ask a question about its actual contents.
7. Use live search and display genuine source citations.
8. Open each implemented tool and test its core functionality.
9. Save and retrieve generated notes or documents.
10. Verify that downloads contain real generated content.
11. Confirm that one user cannot access another user's private records.
12. Check that secrets are not exposed in browser code.
13. Test empty inputs, network failures, API failures, unsupported files, and database errors.
14. Test the responsive interface on desktop and mobile-sized screens.
15. Verify that image generation and video generation are not included.

These are acceptance criteria, not simulated results. Report accurately which checks passed and which require external setup.

